CloudBurrow patch 45 to github.com/goccy/bigquery-emulator v0.8.1
(cloudburrow/cloudburrow#1456).

The bug: a RANGE value inside a RECORD (a STRUCT column holding a
RANGE<TIMESTAMP> field, or a RECORD in a REPEATED RECORD) read back in a
query result as GoogleSQL's text, a TIMESTAMP bound as
"2020-01-01 00:00:00+00" and a DATETIME bound with a space, where
BigQuery's REST API gives int64 microseconds and a "T": patch 0008's Format
rewrote only top-level and REPEATED RANGE values, as Format does not walk
STRUCTs. The official Go client fails to parse such a value.

The patch walks a RECORD cell (and a REPEATED RECORD's cells) whose schema
holds a RANGE at any depth, and writes each RANGE in it with 0008's
formatRangeCells; needs 0008.

